      "writtenOn": "2021-07-07T21:24:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There currently isn\u0027t one.  This function is being called indirectly from dma_buf_detach(), through a call to dma_buf_attach_stats_teardown() (https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common/+/refs/heads/android12-5.10/drivers/dma-buf/dma-buf.c#862), which queues this to be called.  On the android12-5.10 today, the work being done asyncrhonously in dma_buf_attach_stats_do_teardown_work() is just done synchronously in dma_buf_attach_stats_teardown() .\n\nIf we consider the android12-5.10 as it is, such that two parties call dma_buf_attach() on the same attachment concurrently, I think there would still be a race in dma_buf_attach_stats_teardown(): https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common/+/refs/heads/android12-5.10/drivers/dma-buf/dma-buf-sysfs-stats.c#146\n\nThat is, the checks on lines 150-152 on the LHS and lines 165-166 on the RHS should be just as good as one another.",
